  "id": "COMPOUND:23441 - PROTEIN:5841",
  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is proposed to interact with A-431 through a series of molecular targets, primarily the dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is targeted by multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, CID 21778290, and Ascidiathiazone B, all of which are implicated in modulating the activity of the kinase. The presence of multiple targets suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of kinase activity, which could influence cellular processes such as signal transduction and cell proliferation. The integration of these targets into the pathway highlights a possible role for Corticatic Acid E in modulating the kinase activity, thereby affecting A-431. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Corticatic Acid E and A-431, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
